# Algolia Autocomplete for Next.js

Production-ready autocomplete component using `@algolia/autocomplete-js` with Next.js App Router.

## Features

- **Zero-config styling** — Works out of the box with included CSS Modules
- **Fully typed** — TypeScript definitions for hits, props, and callbacks
- **SSR-safe** — Client-only initialization with `use client` directive
- **Customizable** — Override item rendering, URL resolution, and selection handling
- **Mobile-optimized** — Full-screen dropdown on small screens via `detachedMediaQuery`
- **Accessible** — Keyboard navigation, ARIA attributes, focus management built-in

## Installation

```bash
npm install @algolia/autocomplete-js algoliasearch
```

## Usage

```tsx
import { SearchAutocomplete } from "@/components/SearchAutocomplete";

export default function SearchPage() {
  return (
    <SearchAutocomplete
      appId={process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_ALGOLIA_APP_ID!}
      apiKey={process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_ALGOLIA_SEARCH_API_KEY!}
      indexName={process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_ALGOLIA_INDEX_NAME!}
      placeholder="Search docs..."
      maxResults={5}
      onSelect={(hit) => router.push(hit.url)}
    />
  );
}
```

## Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `appId` | `string` | — | Algolia Application ID |
| `apiKey` | `string` | — | Search-only API Key |
| `indexName` | `string` | — | Target index name |
| `placeholder` | `string` | `"Search..."` | Input placeholder text |
| `className` | `string` | `""` | Additional wrapper classes |
| `onSelect` | `(hit: Hit) => void` | — | Callback when item selected |
| `getItemUrl` | `(hit: Hit) => string` | `hit.url` | Custom URL resolver |
| `renderItem` | `(hit, children) => ReactNode` | — | Custom item renderer |
| `maxResults` | `number` | `5` | Hits per query |
| `detachedMediaQuery` | `string` | `"(max-width: 640px)"` | Full-screen breakpoint |
| `openOnFocus` | `boolean` | `true` | Open dropdown on focus |
| `autoFocus` | `boolean` | `false` | Auto-focus on mount |
| `initialQuery` | `string` | `""` | Pre-fill query |
| `stallThreshold` | `number` | `300` | Loading indicator delay (ms) |

## Environment Variables

Copy `.env.example` to `.env.local`:

```env
NEXT_PUBLIC_ALGOLIA_APP_ID=your_app_id
NEXT_PUBLIC_ALGOLIA_SEARCH_API_KEY=your_search_only_api_key
NEXT_PUBLIC_ALGOLIA_INDEX_NAME=your_index_name
```

## Demo

Run the demo page at `/search`:

```bash
npm run dev
```

The demo uses a mock client — replace with real credentials for production.

## Architecture

```
src/
├── components/
│   ├── SearchAutocomplete.tsx      # Main component
│   └── SearchAutocomplete.module.css  # Scoped styles
├── lib/
│   └── algolia.ts                  # Server-side search client
└── app/
    └── search/
        └── page.tsx                # Demo page
```

## Customization

### Custom Item Rendering

```tsx
<SearchAutocomplete
  renderItem={(hit, children) => (
    <div className="custom-item">
      <Badge>{hit.category}</Badge>
      {children}
    </div>
  )}
/>
```

### Multiple Sources

Extend `getSources` in the component to add recent searches, categories, or facet filters.

### Theming

Override CSS custom properties:

```css
:root {
  --aa-background-hover: #f0f4ff;
  --aa-primary: #0066cc;
}
```

